index c01f556132..517784405a 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ Enhancements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 - The metadata returned by :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data` has two new columns: ``dataset``, the code of the dataset each trial comes from (for a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset`, the dataset the subject comes from), and ``device``, the recording device. ``device`` is the canonical name of ``METADATA.acquisition.hardware`` given by :func:`moabb.datasets.metadata.devices.canonical_device` (the 107 free-text descriptions map to 30 devices, e.g. every spelling of the g.tec g.USBamp; ``"unknown"`` when the dataset gives none); :class:`moabb.datasets.Peters2026` returns the DSI-24 or DSI-Flex of each visit. ``CrossSubjectEvaluation(cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut, groups="dataset")`` holds out one dataset at a time and ``groups="device"`` one device at a time, and :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossDatasetSplitter` works on paradigm output (:gh:`1328` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data` no longer fails when the recordings it stacks have different channels or numbers of samples, e.g. datasets with different montages or sampling rates pooled in a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset`: it returns a nested object array of shape ``(n_trials,)`` holding each trial's ``(n_channels, n_times)`` array, and the evaluations accept it, so leave-one-dataset-out runs with :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossSubjectEvaluation` and ``cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut``. Recordings of one shape still give a regular array; ``return_epochs=True`` raises a clear error for such recordings, as ``mne.Epochs`` cannot hold them (:gh:`1327` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- Add opt-in ``PurgedEpochKFold`` for chronological within-recording ERP folds with exact half-open raw-window purging. Pass sample timing and recording identity explicitly as integer-backed ``groups``; evaluation and preprocessing defaults remain unchanged. Continuous-recording filtering can still leak across folds (:gh:`280`, :gh:`1329` by `lindicaphxag-tech`_).
 - Versioned documentation: release tags (``v*``) deploy the "stable" docs to https://moabb.neurotechx.com/docs/ and ``develop`` deploys the "dev" docs to https://moabb.neurotechx.com/dev/, so the default documentation matches the PyPI release; a version switcher in the navbar (``_static/versions.json``) moves between them (:gh:`445`, :gh:`983` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Wang2026` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Han2026` read from NEMAR: PerezBlanco2026 and Wang2026 take the subject's original files from the published deposits ``nm000304`` and ``nm000335`` (``nemar_seed_cache``; Wang2026 declares the deposit's ``sub-<id>`` subject labels), and Han2026 reads NEMAR's raw import of OpenNeuro ds007327 (``on007327``) before OpenNeuro. The private deposits of Brodu2012 (``nm000366``), Lenaig2026 (``nm000333``), MartinezPeon2025 (``nm000332``), MIBMPI2024 (``nm000331``) and MIND2026 (``nm000337``) get their ``nemar_id`` once published (:gh:`1318` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Tavakolan2017`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Liu2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Zhou2020` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Wu2020` take the extracted per-subject tree from the NEMAR store (``fill_tree_from_store``) before downloading the per-subject ZIP, so a subject already mirrored in a deposit loads with no upstream request (:gh:`1313` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
diff --git a/moabb/evaluations/splitters.py b/moabb/evaluations/splitters.py
index 8303596dad..fb365e8211 100644
--- a/moabb/evaluations/splitters.py
+++ b/moabb/evaluations/splitters.py
@@ -1408,3 +1408,152 @@ def get_metadata(self):
             Only valid during or after iteration.
         """
         return {"permutation": self._current_perm, "data_size": self._current_data_size}
+
+
+class PurgedEpochKFold(GroupsConsumerMixin, BaseCrossValidator):
+    """Contiguous within-recording CV without overlapping raw epoch windows.
+
+    Pass groups with three columns: (recording_id, event_sample,
+    epoch_n_samples). Recording IDs must distinguish reused run names across
+    subjects and sessions. Sample starts and lengths must be exact integers;
+    windows are half-open [start, start + length).
+
+    This prevents direct overlap of declared raw epoch extraction windows,
+    *not* leakage through preprocessing of the continuous signal: an IIR
+    filter applied before epoching can couple non-overlapping windows.
+    No automatic paradigm/evaluation integration is performed.
+    """
+
+    def __init__(self, n_splits=5):
+        if (
+            isinstance(n_splits, (bool, np.bool_))
+            or not isinstance(n_splits, (int, np.integer))
+            or n_splits < 2
+        ):
+            raise ValueError("n_splits must be an integer >= 2.")
+        self.n_splits = int(n_splits)
+
+    def get_n_splits(self, X=None, y=None, groups=None):
+        return self.n_splits
+
+    @staticmethod
+    def _parse_groups(groups, n_samples):
+        if groups is None:
+            raise ValueError("PurgedEpochKFold requires explicit epoch timing groups.")
+        values = np.asarray(groups, dtype=object)
+        if values.shape != (n_samples, 3):
+            raise ValueError(
+                "groups must be an (n_epochs, 3) array of "
+                "(recording_id, event_sample, epoch_n_samples)."
+            )
+        # Normalize hashable recording identities to integer codes. Comparing
+        # a NumPy object array against a tuple-valued ID broadcasts the tuple
+        # instead of comparing each complete recording identity.
+        identities = values[:, 0].tolist()
+
+        def missing_identity(value):
+            if value is None:
+                return True
+            if isinstance(value, (float, np.floating)):
+                return bool(np.isnan(value))
+            if isinstance(value, tuple):
+                return any(missing_identity(part) for part in value)
+            return False
+
+        if any(missing_identity(value) for value in identities):
+            raise ValueError("recording_id must not be missing.")
+        recording_codes = {}
+        try:
+            runs = np.fromiter(
+                (
+                    recording_codes.setdefault(value, len(recording_codes))
+                    for value in identities
+                ),
+                dtype=np.intp,
+                count=n_samples,
+            )
+        except TypeError as error:
+            raise ValueError("recording_id must be hashable.") from error
+        limits = np.iinfo(np.int64)
+        parsed = []
+        for column in (values[:, 1], values[:, 2]):
+            ints = []
+            for raw in column:
+                if isinstance(raw, (bool, np.bool_)) or not isinstance(
+                    raw, (int, np.integer)
+                ):
+                    raise ValueError("Epoch sample coordinates must be integers.")
+                value = int(raw)
+                if not limits.min <= value <= limits.max:
+                    raise ValueError("Epoch sample coordinate exceeds int64 range.")
+                ints.append(value)
+            parsed.append(np.asarray(ints, dtype=np.int64))
+        starts, lengths = parsed
+        if np.any(lengths <= 0):
+            raise ValueError("epoch_n_samples must be strictly positive.")
+        if np.any(starts > limits.max - lengths):
+            raise ValueError("Epoch interval stop exceeds int64 range.")
+        return runs, starts, lengths
+
+    @staticmethod
+    def _overlap_mask(train_start, train_stop, test_start, test_stop):
+        """Exact half-open intersection in O((N+M) log M), linear memory."""
+        if not len(train_start) or not len(test_start):
+            return np.zeros(len(train_start), dtype=bool)
+        order = np.argsort(test_start, kind="stable")
+        sorted_starts = test_start[order]
+        max_stop = np.maximum.accumulate(test_stop[order])
+        before = np.searchsorted(sorted_starts, train_stop, side="left")
+        overlaps = before > 0
+        overlaps[overlaps] = max_stop[before[overlaps] - 1] > train_start[overlaps]
+        return overlaps
+
+    def split(self, X, y=None, groups=None):
+        n_samples = len(X)
+        if n_samples < self.n_splits:
+            raise ValueError("Not enough epochs for requested folds.")
+        runs, starts, lengths = self._parse_groups(groups, n_samples)
+        y = None if y is None else np.asarray(y)
+        if y is not None and len(y) != n_samples:
+            raise ValueError("y must contain one label per epoch.")
+
+        # Chronological blocks within each recording. No class-balanced DP:
+        # fail closed if a contiguous fold cannot support every class.
+        run_blocks = []
+        for run in dict.fromkeys(runs.tolist()):
+            indices = np.flatnonzero(runs == run)
+            if len(indices) < self.n_splits:
+                raise ValueError("Each recording needs at least n_splits epochs.")
+            chronological = indices[np.lexsort((indices, starts[indices]))]
+            run_blocks.append((run, np.array_split(chronological, self.n_splits)))
+
+        for fold in range(self.n_splits):
+            test = np.sort(np.concatenate([blocks[fold] for _, blocks in run_blocks]))
+            testing = np.zeros(n_samples, dtype=bool)
+            testing[test] = True
+            purged = np.zeros(n_samples, dtype=bool)
+            for run, _ in run_blocks:
+                local_test = test[runs[test] == run]
+                local_train = np.flatnonzero((runs == run) & ~testing)
+                train_start = starts[local_train]
+                test_start = starts[local_test]
+                purged[
+                    local_train[
+                        self._overlap_mask(
+                            train_start,
+                            train_start + lengths[local_train],
+                            test_start,
+                            test_start + lengths[local_test],
+                        )
+                    ]
+                ] = True
+            train = np.flatnonzero(~testing & ~purged)
+            if not len(train) or not len(test):
+                raise ValueError("Purging removed an entire train or test fold.")
+            if y is not None:
+                required = np.unique(y)
+                if len(np.unique(y[train])) != len(required) or len(
+                    np.unique(y[test])
+                ) != len(required):
+                    raise ValueError("A purged fold lacks a class in train or test.")
+            yield train, test
diff --git a/moabb/tests/test_purged_epoch_minimal.py b/moabb/tests/test_purged_epoch_minimal.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..6769306e0b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/moabb/tests/test_purged_epoch_minimal.py
@@ -0,0 +1,156 @@
+"""Opt-in raw-window overlap CV; does not certify independence after IIR."""
+
+import numpy as np
+import pytest
+
+from moabb.evaluations.splitters import PurgedEpochKFold
+
+
+def _groups(starts, width, recording_ids=None):
+    n = len(starts)
+    groups = np.empty((n, 3), dtype=object)
+    groups[:, 0] = ["one"] * n if recording_ids is None else recording_ids
+    groups[:, 1] = list(starts)
+    groups[:, 2] = [width] * n
+    return groups
+
+
+def _has_overlap(train, test, groups):
+    return any(
+        groups[i, 0] == groups[j, 0]
+        and groups[i, 1] < groups[j, 1] + groups[j, 2]
+        and groups[j, 1] < groups[i, 1] + groups[i, 2]
+        for i in train
+        for j in test
+    )
+
+
+def test_complete_chronological_partition_with_exact_purge():
+    groups = _groups(np.arange(30) * 100, 500)
+    y = np.tile([0, 1], 15)
+    folds = list(PurgedEpochKFold(5).split(np.zeros(30), y, groups))
+    assert sorted(np.concatenate([test for _, test in folds])) == list(range(30))
+    assert len(folds) == 5
+    for train, test in folds:
+        assert not _has_overlap(train, test, groups)
+        assert set(y[train]) == {0, 1}
+        assert set(y[test]) == {0, 1}
+
+
+def test_half_open_touching_boundaries_are_not_purged():
+    actual = PurgedEpochKFold._overlap_mask(
+        np.array([0, 10, 20]), np.array([10, 20, 30]), np.array([10]), np.array([20])
+    )
+    assert actual.tolist() == [False, True, False]
+
+
+def test_independent_recordings_can_reuse_sample_coordinates():
+    groups = _groups(list(np.arange(8) * 800) * 2, 500, ["A"] * 8 + ["B"] * 8)
+    for train, test in PurgedEpochKFold(4).split(np.zeros(16), groups=groups):
+        assert len(test) == 4
+        assert len(train) == 12
+        assert not _has_overlap(train, test, groups)
+
+
+def test_tuple_recording_ids_are_atomic_with_reused_run_labels():
+    # Subject/session/run is naturally a tuple, not an array dimension.
+    labels = [(1, "session-0", "run-0")] * 8 + [(2, "session-0", "run-0")] * 8
+    groups = _groups(list(np.arange(8) * 800) * 2, 500, labels)
+    folds = list(PurgedEpochKFold(4).split(np.zeros(16), groups=groups))
+    assert len(folds) == 4
+    for train, test in folds:
+        assert len(train) == 12
+        assert len(test) == 4
+        assert not _has_overlap(train, test, groups)
+
+
+def test_missing_nan_recording_ids_fail_before_grouping():
+    starts = np.arange(8) * 200
+    for missing_ids in (
+        [np.nan] * 8,
+        [float("nan") for _ in range(8)],
+        [("subject", np.float64("nan"), "run")] * 8,
+        [None] * 8,
+    ):
+        groups = _groups(starts, 100, missing_ids)
+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="recording_id must not be missing"):
+            list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(8), groups=groups))
+
+
+def test_unhashable_recording_id_fails_with_clear_error():
+    groups = _groups(np.arange(8) * 200, 100)
+    groups[0, 0] = ["subject", "run"]
+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="hashable"):
+        list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(8), groups=groups))
+
+
+def test_chronology_is_not_assumed_from_dataframe_row_order():
+    starts = np.random.default_rng(1).permutation(np.arange(20) * 500)
+    groups = _groups(starts, 400)
+    folds = list(PurgedEpochKFold(4).split(np.zeros(20), groups=groups))
+    assert sorted(np.concatenate([test for _, test in folds])) == list(range(20))
+    for _, test in folds:
+        positions = np.searchsorted(np.sort(starts), starts[test])
+        assert sorted(positions) == list(range(min(positions), max(positions) + 1))
+
+
+def test_only_exact_integer_coordinates_and_no_int64_overflow():
+    groups = _groups(np.arange(8) * 200, 100)
+    for invalid in (0.5, 1.0, True, "1"):
+        malformed = groups.copy()
+        malformed[0, 1] = invalid
+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="integers"):
+            list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(8), groups=malformed))
+    shifted = groups.copy()
+    shifted[:, 1] = [int(x) + 2**53 + 101 for x in groups[:, 1]]
+    a = list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(8), groups=groups))
+    b = list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(8), groups=shifted))
+    for (train_a, test_a), (train_b, test_b) in zip(a, b):
+        np.testing.assert_array_equal(train_a, train_b)
+        np.testing.assert_array_equal(test_a, test_b)
+    overflow = groups.copy()
+    overflow[0, 1] = 2**63 - 1
+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="stop exceeds"):
+        list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(8), groups=overflow))
+
+
+def test_missing_inputs_and_unsupported_class_partition_fail_closed():
+    groups = _groups(np.arange(10) * 800, 500)
+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="explicit epoch timing"):
+        list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(10)))
+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="shape|array"):
+        list(PurgedEpochKFold(2).split(np.zeros(10), groups=np.ones((10, 2))))
+    labels = np.array([0] * 8 + [1] * 2)
+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="lacks a class"):
+        list(PurgedEpochKFold(5).split(np.zeros(10), labels, groups))
+
+
+def test_prefix_max_interval_search_equals_independent_dense_oracle():
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(20261025)
+    for _ in range(150):
+        train_start = rng.integers(-20, 90, size=35)
+        train_stop = train_start + rng.integers(1, 30, size=35)
+        test_start = rng.integers(-20, 90, size=25)
+        test_stop = test_start + rng.integers(1, 30, size=25)
+        observed = PurgedEpochKFold._overlap_mask(
+            train_start, train_stop, test_start, test_stop
+        )
+        expected = (
+            (train_start[:, None] < test_stop[None, :])
+            & (test_start[None, :] < train_stop[:, None])
+        ).any(axis=1)
+        np.testing.assert_array_equal(observed, expected)
+
+
+def test_large_cohort_has_no_quadratic_overlap_matrix():
+    n = 30000
+    starts = np.arange(n, dtype=np.int64) * 4
+    actual = PurgedEpochKFold._overlap_mask(starts + 1, starts + 3, starts, starts + 2)
+    assert actual.shape == (n,)
+    assert actual.all()
+
+
+def test_docstring_preserves_filtering_limitation():
+    doc = PurgedEpochKFold.__doc__
+    assert "IIR" in doc
+    assert "not" in doc.lower()
